  "prompt": "Mailvora's marketing manager reads December 2025's purchases by first-touch medium from the export. Check them against the backend. On the export side, count the purchase events of the Dublin days 1 to 31 December (by event_date), grouped by traffic_source.medium, the visitor's first touch. On the backend side, count the subscriptions whose first payment (earliest paid_at) falls on those Dublin days, a first payment that was later refunded included, grouped by the utm_medium of the first session (earliest session_start) of the visitor who signed up as that subscription's user, with a missing utm_medium read as (none). Return four columns, in this order: medium, export_purchases, backend_first_payments and difference (export_purchases minus backend_first_payments). Return one row for each medium that either side has, with 0 where a side has none. Any row order is fine.",
